{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The&nbsp;proposed development fails to provide sufficient information with respect to waste management and storage, the provision and management of car parking and adequate cycle storage. In the absence of information to the contrary,&nbsp; the proposal is likely to result in a harmful increase in parking stress to the area. The proposal fails to demonstrate safe and adequate car parking. The storage and servicing of waste management conflicts with the proposed cycle parking spaces and would limit opportunities for sustainable travel. The proposal is therefore likely to result in a detrimental impact on highway safety and the existing transport network, and runs contrary to&nbsp;sustainable travel principles. It is therefore contrary to the following: - The National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)- Policies T3, T5 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)-&nbsp;Policies SP8, DMM1, DMS1, DMSI 8, DMT2; and - DMT3 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037&nbsp;(September 2024)-&nbsp;Planning Advice Note on Waste and Recycling Provisions in New and Refurbished Residential Developments (May 2021)&nbsp;",
    "The&amp;nbsp;proposed flat would fail provide any private external amenity space and would result in the provision of a poorly designed dwelling in a sub-standard location.&amp;nbsp; Additionally, the proposal has failed to adequately demonstrate that the flat would receive adequate levels of sunlight, further exacerbating the poor design of the flat and contributing to a sub-standard quality of accommodation of poor design.&amp;nbsp;It is therefore contrary to:The National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024)DCLG Technical Housing Standards (nationally described space standard) (DCLG, March 2015) (as amended)Policies&amp;nbsp;D6,&amp;nbsp; H1, H2 and Table 3.1 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy SP3, DMD 1 and Part 6 of Policy DMNE1 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan 2037 (September 2024)Housing Design Standards LPG (June 2023)"
  ],
